g; Hello, JNI/FFM application tests and Minecraft did not run. R5 has passed 92 Switchcraft host tests, 23 runtime host tests, class-library regressions, genuine instrumented Minecraft-profile cross-build/link, source/package reconstruction and final package checks. These are host/build results. **R5 Horizon execution remains NOT TESTED; no Switch Minecraft title is claimed.**\n\nDownload only `switchcraft-test-suite-2026-11-13-r5.zip` for SD installation. Extract it into the SD root, merge directories and preserve existing saves/configuration. Begin with one fresh application-mode `java25-test` A. If it does not capture actual Hello output and stage `completed`, stop dependent Java tests and export logs. Otherwise follow the included START_HERE.md; each Java choice needs a fresh process. Source, debug and SDK assets stay off the SD card.\n\nVerified minimal Switchcraft device test package `switchcraft-test-suite-2026-11-13-r5.zip`.\n\nSHA-256: `008b93e3af2cbb26ed3069f4d5ad336f2721f30256a972ad517a8aa96c0a5a98` (54717758 bytes).\n\nThis R5 ZIP is ready to extract directly onto the SD root. Use application-mode hbmenu and the included START_HERE.md. Start with a fresh standalone Java 25 A attempt; every Java 25 action requires its own process.\n\nPhysical execution is NOT TESTED until fresh Switch logs establish results. Cross-builds and host tests do not establish Java, JNI/FFM, instrumentation, graphics or Minecraft execution.\n\nRequired separate source companion: `switchcraft-source-2026-11-13-r5.tar.gz` (152423762 bytes, SHA-256 `18611a3a1df28c3a8bd1487738996f473410cd9bbb1fd15eb715ea5b562437ac`).\n\nOptional asset: `switchcraft-debug-symbols-2026-11-13-r5.zip` (57491035 bytes, SHA-256 `5037d154ad2f6fa6f5addd7b239036c206b3067151290fe4e4299aa58947f78e`).\n\nOptional asset: `switchcraft-native-sdk-2026-11-13-r5.tar.gz` (25477597 bytes, SHA-256 `deb2eed33122d84cd411dfed9e539f9386ac0ff6a0d0ec0d679f3fee98a53efb`).\n\nOptional asset: `switchcraft-r5-validation.txt` (133